  "result": "I haven't changed any code yet. Plan mode is on and I can't exit it here, so I've only written the plan.\n\n**Cause:** in `src/click/core.py:386-394`, a subcommand's context copies its parent's whole `default_map`. It should take only the entry for its own name. With `default_map={\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}`, the `runserver` context looks for `port` in the outer dict, finds nothing, and ignores the default.\n\n**Fix:** change `default_map = parent.default_map` to `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. The `info_name is not None` check is already there. If the parent map has no entry for the subcommand, the child gets no `default_map`, which is how it behaves today when none is set.\n\n**Also planned:**\n- Add tests in `tests/test_defaults.py`. They cover a subcommand picking up its default, a CLI argument overriding it, and a nested group.\n- Add a `CHANGES.md` entry.\n- Run `tests/test_defaults.py`, `tests/test_context.py` and `tests/test_options.py`, then the full suite.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-glistening-pancake.md`. Tell me to proceed and I'll make the edits.",
